{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1291597-true-resurrection-this-shouldn-t-work-but-how","id":1291597,"title":"True Resurrection: this shouldn't work but how?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-24T13:51:00-08:00","id":1291597,"title":"True Resurrection: this shouldn't work but how?","content":"Ignoring just timetravelling to prevent the death in the first place, a Death 5 Time 5 mage could use Time to make an arbitrary corpse &quot;recently dead&quot; and use Death to fix/resurrect the dead body. Most importantly though, they could use Time and Death to retrieve the soul of the deceased from the past before their death. So that <i>could </i>be a full complete resurrection. <br /> <br /> It shouldn't be though. I just can't think of how","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T14:14:46-08:00","id":1291606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lareath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1291597-true-resurrection-this-shouldn-t-work-but-how#post1291597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ignoring just timetravelling to prevent the death in the first place, a Death 5 Time 5 mage could use Time to make an arbitrary corpse &quot;recently dead&quot; and use Death to fix/resurrect the dead body. Most importantly though, they could use Time and Death to retrieve the soul of the deceased from the past before their death. So that <i>could </i>be a full complete resurrection.<br /> <br /> It shouldn't be though. I just can't think of how</div> </div> </div> </div>Retrieving the soul of the deceased from the past literally isn't going to work without time travel in the first place, and both resurrecting the body and reattaching the soul require maintaining additional spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T14:30:14-08:00","id":1291612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1291597-true-resurrection-this-shouldn-t-work-but-how?p=1291606#post1291606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Retrieving the soul of the deceased from the past literally isn't going to work without time travel in the first place, and both resurrecting the body and reattaching the soul require maintaining additional spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ... don't see how this is an objection?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T14:35:53-08:00","id":1291614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lareath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1291597-true-resurrection-this-shouldn-t-work-but-how?p=1291612#post1291612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ... don't see how this is an objection?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you're not being terribly clear about what you're asking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T14:37:26-08:00","id":1291615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lareath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1291597-true-resurrection-this-shouldn-t-work-but-how?p=1291612#post1291612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ... don't see how this is an objection?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there some framework you had in mind where discounting the simple plan of traveling back in time to prevent the death is necessary but traveling back in time to steal the target's soul ahead of time is totally fine?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T14:38:21-08:00","id":1291616,"title":"","content":"The text of Mage seems to imply (to me anyway) that souls of the deceased go on to transcend the boundaries of the Fallen World, which could mean that once someone dies, their soul can no longer be retrieved from any point in time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":". 02-24-2019, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T15:17:50-08:00","id":1291629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1291597-true-resurrection-this-shouldn-t-work-but-how?p=1291616#post1291616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The text of Mage seems to imply (to me anyway) that souls of the deceased go on to transcend the boundaries of the Fallen World, which could mean that once someone dies, their soul can no longer be retrieved from any point in time.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that were true then using Shifting Sands to go back an hour in the past to save your cabal mate and prevent them from dying would leave them soulless, which is something I think would have been mentioned somewhere either in the spell or in the general introduction to how Time works. As it is I'm pretty sure that whatever souls do after death is still bound by time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T18:14:41-08:00","id":1291672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1291597-true-resurrection-this-shouldn-t-work-but-how?p=1291629#post1291629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that were true then using Shifting Sands to go back an hour in the past to save your cabal mate and prevent them from dying would leave them soulless, which is something I think would have been mentioned somewhere either in the spell or in the general introduction to how Time works. As it is I'm pretty sure that whatever souls do after death is still bound by time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, fair point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T21:48:03-08:00","id":1291721,"title":"","content":"I had this impression as well! I can't remember why though. It feels like it came from somewhere buried in 1st Edition...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T03:23:17-08:00","id":1291768,"title":"","content":"You could technically do all of this, but why would you bother setting this up if you're already capable of time travelling to a point before the subject's demise and thus being capable of just preventing their death outright?<br /> One of the drawbacks of doing this would be that you're forced to use at least one non-Lasting spell which, if undone, will straight up kill the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T05:31:35-08:00","id":1291795,"title":"","content":"Not to mention the fact that the spell holding the person alive has to be maintained; if it is dispelled the person dies again. So yeah, just go back in time and prevent the death in the first place. I guarantee you that it is far less hassle (with the exception that the ST can, if he wants to, make it more hassle).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T05:43:22-08:00","id":1291796,"title":"","content":"That's the spell I meant, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T12:51:16-08:00","id":1291913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>this shouldn't work</b><br /> </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> <br /> It's more convoluted than just preventing the death in the first place, and only has disadvantages compared to that other, easier method. Even if that weren't the case, though, I'm having trouble understanding the premise of this being a thing that should be impossible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T03:27:00-08:00","id":1292104,"title":"","content":"This is no where near true resurrection. It's not a lasting effect, so you'll need to maintain the spells, or at the very least spend willpower dot just to relinquish the effects, which can then be easily dispelled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 02-26-2019, 06:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T14:49:28-08:00","id":1292268,"title":"","content":"Aren't souls fairly interchangeable anyway? Making the corpse recently dead, fix it with death, and sticking any old soul into it could work without the time travel right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T16:07:01-08:00","id":1292279,"title":"","content":"I can't believe I'm about to say this, but wouldn't it be easier to just time travel the death away and then kite it forward until it becomes lasting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T08:38:13-08:00","id":1292501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can't believe I'm about to say this, but wouldn't it be easier to just time travel the death away and then kite it forward until it becomes lasting? </div> </div> </div>Yes. *if* your character is a Master of Time, and not a Master of Death. <br /> In my game, one of the PCs has decided that his first order of business as a Master of Death will be to bring back his dead mother. She died 7 years ago, which means at the rate of one month per Potency he'd need to cast a Potency 84 spell, not counting other factors such as duration. The player then considered getting help, being sent back in time to near the moment when the PCs mom died, grabbing her soul at the moment of death and storing it in a soul jar. Then resurrecting her that same day, at a much lower potency, and putting her own soul back in her (just so that he didn't have to go looking/trading for a 'loose' one someplace else).<br /> As ST, I pointed out that this would effectively re-write 7 years of her character's backstory, as the PC would not lose his mother at a young age, etc. <br /> So, she plans to have her character instead go back in time, grab the soul, grab the body after burial ( #MorosLife ) and bring them back to the present-day before resurrecting. That way, life goes on for 7 years as if the PC's mom was dead, as before, but he has the chance to bring her back, with just a 7-year gap in her mind between when she was dying (and her son was a teen) to the day she is resurrected by her 20-something, Master of Death son. <br /> PS Mom's a Proximus of a homebrew line derived from the Travellers of the UK and Ireland. So Dissonance is not an issue on her part, even if she finds out she was actually dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/550-redline","name":"Redline","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T12:06:22-08:00","id":1292562,"title":"","content":"The premise of the thread was a theoretical character with mastery in both Time and Death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T12:45:26-08:00","id":1292577,"title":"","content":"Nah, if the character is going back in time anyways then he should just go back before the person died and prevent the death...unless the death is due to old age. However, since it doesn't seem to be due to old age, just preventing the death in the first place seems much easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T00:02:30-08:00","id":1293250,"title":"","content":"This thread has been quite helpful, thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T04:53:14-08:00","id":1293280,"title":"","content":"In that we've pointed out the drawbacks (making it not an unconditional full resurrection whatwith the non-Lasting spells) or that we've changed your mind in whether it should be possible or not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T12:49:29-08:00","id":1293528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1291597-true-resurrection-this-shouldn-t-work-but-how?p=1293280#post1293280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that we've pointed out the drawbacks (making it not an unconditional full resurrection whatwith the non-Lasting spells) or that we've changed your mind in whether it should be possible or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>It helped clarify my thoughts on &quot;yes this is technically doable&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3642,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","user":"Lareath","date":". 03-03-2019, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T10:25:55-08:00","id":1294102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lareath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1291597-true-resurrection-this-shouldn-t-work-but-how?p=1293528#post1293528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It helped clarify my thoughts on &quot;yes this is technically doable&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This got longer than I inteded so TL;DR is if one method can do it, then another should also be able to. That does not mean though, that there should not be consequences and side effects, otherwise this is something NPC's would be doing all the time.<br /> <br /> I'd argue it this way; if one method of doing something will work (i.e. time travel to prevent death) the another method should also work. Once you've established that the resurrection is possible, the means are just details. Personally though, as a ST, I'd use it as a lesson in why <i>everyone</i> doesn't just do that. I'd let it happen, and demonstrate the consequences for doing it. If the players can do it, then so can NPC's, which means it would be happening all the time. If it's not happening all the time, there's a reason for it, probably to do with consequences for trying it. <br /> His mother was supposed to die, he is trying to save her, why would Death let her live again? Her soul has already made it's way beyond the Lie and to whatever awaits it down the line. Your PC found a way to cheat Death, personally, as a ST, Death would not take kindly to that. <br /> Someone mentioned (I'm too lazy to go back and look at who) that once someone dies their soul exits the Fallen World, the counter argument was that you can definitely rewind the last few turns to prevent death without consequence. This to me, does not contradict the first statement. What if the soul does leave the Fallen World (and therefore can't be reattached) but doesn't do so immediately? Effectively waiting to make sure no shenanigans return it to it's body before moving on, but once it has moved on, it's gone. Perhaps this means it works for a while but the soul doesn't remain attached properly? Or maybe Fate conspires to have the mother killed again?<br /> <br /> In summary, this is something I would let players attempt to do, it is not something I would let them do easily, freely, or without fallout. It would likely bite them in the ass, and hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23958-tengugrib","name":"TenguGrib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T10:55:19-08:00","id":1294108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TenguGrib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1291597-true-resurrection-this-shouldn-t-work-but-how?p=1294102#post1294102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This got longer than I inteded so TL;DR is if one method can do it, then another should also be able to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where this runs aground is that &quot;retrieving the soul from the past&quot; doesn't work without traveling back in time to a point where the soul was still around, at which point you might as well just prevent the death in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T11:46:41-08:00","id":1294120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1291597-true-resurrection-this-shouldn-t-work-but-how?p=1294108#post1294108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where this runs aground is that &quot;retrieving the soul from the past&quot; doesn't work without traveling back in time to a point where the soul was still around, at which point you might as well just prevent the death in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree because preventing the death will cause repercussions in the timeline, perhaps severe ones. Snatching the soul away at the moment of death and bringing it back to the present will skip all the problems that arise because his mother never died.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23958-tengugrib","name":"TenguGrib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T12:10:23-08:00","id":1294124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TenguGrib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1291597-true-resurrection-this-shouldn-t-work-but-how?p=1294120#post1294120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree because preventing the death will cause repercussions in the timeline, perhaps severe ones. Snatching the soul away at the moment of death and bringing it back to the present will skip all the problems that arise because his mother never died.</div> </div> </div> </div>And at <i>that</i> point you might as well just suppress her life indefinitely or shunt her into the future and save yourself the trouble of juggling spell control. You think casting a spell on somebody in the past isn't going to have its own repercussions already?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T16:21:49-08:00","id":1294206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1291597-true-resurrection-this-shouldn-t-work-but-how?p=1294124#post1294124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And at <i>that</i> point you might as well just suppress her life indefinitely or shunt her into the future and save yourself the trouble of juggling spell control. You think casting a spell on somebody in the past isn't going to have its own repercussions already?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course it will, which is my entire point. No matter how you attempt to do this, the consequences should be significant enough that it becomes clear why people don't just do this all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23958-tengugrib","name":"TenguGrib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T16:50:25-08:00","id":1294222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TenguGrib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1291597-true-resurrection-this-shouldn-t-work-but-how?p=1294120#post1294120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree because preventing the death will cause repercussions in the timeline, perhaps severe ones. Snatching the soul away at the moment of death and bringing it back to the present will skip all the problems that arise because his mother never died.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this presupposes a lot of things that are not there to presuppose(Including but not limited to &quot;Does the mage bothering with this entire debacle <i>care</i> about the problems that arise because some mother didn't die?&quot;), but I also kind of have to point out that the nature of Time in Awakening means that this is a non-starter anyways. Stick a wedge in the rope to keep the target from dying before the pattern of living becomes Lasting, and the rest of the metaphysics more or less handles the rest since the timeline will otherwise try to play reality as close as possible to what happened up to the present otherwise. If the person made alive again is just that entangled with their mother that they end up living by virtue of the target living, it's still mostly not a big deal. Radical reformations of history are the domain of Imperial Mysteries, not the standard effect of Time.<br /> <br /> It's only the lives of people. Not so big a deal for the sort of person who reshuffles the deck of history for their own winning hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-05-2019, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T21:03:32-08:00","id":1294310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TenguGrib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1291597-true-resurrection-this-shouldn-t-work-but-how?p=1294206#post1294206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course it will, which is my entire point. No matter how you attempt to do this, the consequences should be significant enough that it becomes clear why people don't just do this all the time</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026There's <i>already</i> a very clear reason why people don't just do this all the time.<br /> <br /> That reason is &quot;double Mastery requires at least Gnosis 6 and tutelage by at least one other Master (a role limited by the individual Arcanum to specific Paths or Legacies), and also this plan requires dedicating two separate spells for restoring a corpse to a viable state and restoring life to that conditionally-recently-dead body as an ongoing process that each require their own investment of will to remove the strain on such a mage's spellcasting resources.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mastery is not commonplace!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T23:53:48-08:00","id":1294984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1291597-true-resurrection-this-shouldn-t-work-but-how?p=1294108#post1294108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where this runs aground is that &quot;retrieving the soul from the past&quot; doesn't work without traveling back in time to a point where the soul was still around, at which point you might as well just prevent the death in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been letting statements like this go by since I didn't want to derail my own question but now my curiosity has gotten the better of me: what is the basis for this assertion that retrieving something from the past requires personally travelling into the past? Especially given spells like Temporal Summoning and Alter History?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T00:11:16-08:00","id":1294986,"title":"","content":"I hate to derail this further but would a thyrsus need spirit 5 or 6 in order to study and reverse engineer a numina that ressurects the dead? I'd fancy 6 or even 7 but, if a thysus finds a spirit that has the numen (and im guessing dread powers do not count) can a thyrsus just study the numen? Or if the dread power belonged to a Claimed creature?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T01:22:52-08:00","id":1294995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1291597-true-resurrection-this-shouldn-t-work-but-how?p=1294986#post1294986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate to derail this further but would a thyrsus need spirit 5 or 6 in order to study and reverse engineer a numina that ressurects the dead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I'm misunderstanding you, but it's 4 dots. Shape Spirit lets you add numen. The difficulty is that Resurrection requires a 4+ rank spirit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd fancy 6 or even 7 but, if a thysus finds a spirit that has the numen (and im guessing dread powers do not count) can a thyrsus just study the numen? Or if the dread power belonged to a Claimed creature? </div> </div> </div>At least in 1e, I think it was 7 that let you create entirely new numina.<br /> <br /> The real underlying problem I think is that the Spirit arcana works with something that isn't real, so it's fairly arbitrary what the ST thinks Numina can and can't do. Like, resurrection is only available for +4 rank spirits... but there's no real indication of why this is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T17:46:28-08:00","id":1295166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lareath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1291597-true-resurrection-this-shouldn-t-work-but-how?p=1294984#post1294984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been letting statements like this go by since I didn't want to derail my own question but now my curiosity has gotten the better of me: what is the basis for this assertion that retrieving something from the past requires personally travelling into the past? Especially given spells like Temporal Summoning and Alter History?</div> </div> </div> </div>The way that Temporal Sympathy works \u2014 i.e. the mechanic that you would need to engage with to meaningfully retrieve a soul after it has vanished \u2014 requires that any spell you're using the Attainment with be either a Time spell that specifically calls for it or a spell combined with one of those spells.<br /> <br /> To quote a breakdown I already did for this topic:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/936233-mechanical-errata-opp-blog?p=939367#post939367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can send a subject back in time through temporal sympathy because temporal sympathy is &quot;things have a connection to the way they used to be.&quot; <i>There is no &quot;used to be&quot; for spells</i>. Momentary Flux and Postcognition are spells that look at a point in time and do nothing else aside from maybe offering a vector for other investigatory spells to be used - Temporal Sympathy extends their range because it's basically pulling copies of established information forward, not because there's suddenly a Time Probe floating around in the past.<br /> <br /> I have elsewhere repeated the sentiments of &quot;changing the past requires time travel&quot; and &quot;the mechanics for noticing when someone or something is trying to change the past through time travel do not exist purely for the purposes of ignoring them as you toss butterfly-effect bombs into the past from the present or are stopped by the ST from doing so through fiat alone&quot; and &quot;there is an entire section at the front of the Time Arcanum writeup before the description of Temporal Sympathy that frames time travel as a thing that moves a subject back to places it's already been and any spell you cast by definition has no sympathy with the time before you cast it.&quot;<br /> <br /> The game takes place in the present, provides rules for going to the established past, and offers a quality of temporal magic that interacts with the notion that the past can be repeated in the present through memories and similar records. The more unfamiliar a point in the past is to its subject, the harder it is to bring that past to the subject or send the subject to that past; spells only properly exist within the span of their Duration, not after and not before, which means you can't cast a spell that starts before you actually cast it.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T20:15:05-08:00","id":1295198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1291597-true-resurrection-this-shouldn-t-work-but-how?p=1295166#post1295166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way that Temporal Sympathy works \u2014 i.e. the mechanic that you would need to engage with to meaningfully retrieve a soul after it has vanished \u2014 requires that any spell you're using the Attainment with be either a Time spell that specifically calls for it or a spell combined with one of those spells.<br /> <br /> To quote a breakdown I already did for this topic:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, that's actually quite insightful and helpful","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}